From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:04:17 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 22/45] lanes: price a block head's pass per drafting stream

A DSpark block costs one pass whatever its depth, and Inkling 2 runs
those passes a stream at a time. Shared rounds priced drafts by depth
past each stream's first, so every stream's first draft looked free and
four or eight streams kept drafting at ~16 ms a stream for ~0.5 tokens.
With draft_passes set, the allocator charges draft_step_ms once a
drafting stream, and the measured overhead leaves those passes out.
